# example_library.agg
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shared DecL knowledge base for the aggregate Example Library.
#
# Define canonical, reusable objects here ONCE; reference them from posts by
# name (sev.Name, agg.Name). Change an assumption here and every example that
# references it updates -- a single source of truth for shared assumptions.
#
# Posts load this file into their own Underwriter:
#     uw = Underwriter(databases=None)
#     uw.load('example_library.agg')
#     a = uw.build('agg MyBook agg.SampleBook occurrence net of 50 xs 50')
#
# Principle: DRY in the source, explicit in the render. Reuse the definition by
# name, but qd() the referenced object on the page so the reader still sees the
# assumptions (see README.md).
#
# Naming: PascalCase, descriptive. Keep this file small and curated -- only
# objects genuinely shared across posts belong here; one-off models live inline
# in their post.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- canonical severities --------------------------------------------------
sev Unit          dsev [1]            note{degenerate severity, always 1; handy for pure frequency studies};
sev MedLognorm    lognorm 100 cv 2    note{medium-tailed reference severity, mean 100 CV 2};

# --- canonical aggregates --------------------------------------------------
agg SampleBook    100 claims sev.MedLognorm poisson    note{reference Poisson x lognormal book};
